      "content": "Adding 5 and 7 gives 12, and dividing by 2 gives 6.\n\n**Final Answer:** $6$\n\n---\n### 📖 Formula Breakdown (How It Works):\n* **The Rule / Formula:** $\\text{Median} = \\frac{\\text{Middle}_1 + \\text{Middle}_2}{2}$\n* **What the terms mean:**\n  * $\\text{Middle}_1$: The lower of the two middle values when data is sorted (here: $5$)\n  * $\\text{Middle}_2$: The upper of the two middle values when data is sorted (here: $7$)\n* **Why we use it:** When a dataset has an even number of items ($n$ is even), there is no single center number. We use the **M.I.D.** mnemonic (**M**eet **I**n the **D**efinite middle, **D**ivide by 2) to find the exact halfway point between the two middle numbers.\n\n🎯 **Exam Tip:** Always check if the dataset is ordered from smallest to largest *before* finding the median. If you forget to sort the data first, you will pick the wrong numbers and lose all the marks!"
